-- title:
--   Galois invariance on norm-one ideles extends to all ideles
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subseteq L$ be number fields, $L$ an algebra over $K$, and let $D$ be an idele Galois descent datum for $\mathcal{O}_L$, $K$, $L$: that is, a monoid homomorphism $g \mapsto D.\mathrm{act}\,g$ from $L \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K]} L$ to the ring automorphisms of the adele ring $\mathbb{A}_L$ of $L$, such that each $D.\mathrm{act}\,g$ is compatible with $g$ on principal adeles, $D.\mathrm{act}\,g\,(\iota x) = \iota(g x)$ for $x \in L$, and such that each $D.\mathrm{act}\,g$ is continuous. Fix $\sigma \in L \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K]} L$ and write `D.unitsAct σ` for the multiplicative automorphism of the idele group $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ obtained by restricting the ring automorphism $D.\mathrm{act}\,\sigma$ to units. Let $M$ be a commutative group and $\xi \colon \mathbb{A}_L^\times \to M$ a group homomorphism, with no continuity and no condition on principal ideles assumed. Suppose that $\xi$ is $\sigma$-invariant on the subgroup [`NumberField.TateGlobal.normOneIdeles L`](def/NumberField_TateGlobalZeta.html#L16), the kernel of the distributional Haar character of $\mathbb{A}_L$ on its unit group, i.e. $\xi(D.\mathrm{unitsAct}\,\sigma\,z) = \xi(z)$ for all $z$ in that kernel. Then $\xi(D.\mathrm{unitsAct}\,\sigma\,z) = \xi(z)$ for every idele $z \in \mathbb{A}_L^\times$.
--
--   This is the statement that the coboundary character $z \mapsto \xi(\sigma z)\xi(z)^{-1}$ of an abstract character of the idele group is trivial as soon as it is trivial on the norm-one ideles, the point being that the idelic norm admits a continuous splitting, so that $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ is generated by the norm-one ideles together with the image of that splitting. It is used where only Galois-invariant central characters are allowed to contribute, namely in the decomposition of a $\sigma$-twist of an idele character into a power of the norm character and in the vanishing and Maass–Selberg statements for adelic integrals of automorphic forms.
-- source:
